[FDE] Gemini Enterprise BYO-MCP: SharePoint Integration
schedule
2 hours
universal_currency_alt
7 Credits
info
This lab may incorporate AI tools to support your learning.
L400-APEX005
Scenario
Cymbal Group, a multinational services company, is rolling out Gemini Enterprise to improve knowledge discovery, operational efficiency, and cross-platform collaboration.

Currently, Cymbal Group is undergoing a massive digital transformation to modernize how its global teams interact with internal operational playbooks, cross-department marketing initiatives, and critical financial ledgers. Because these assets are currently spread across fragmented Microsoft SharePoint team sites and OneDrive repositories, employees are forced to manually toggle between multiple applications to find information, look up technical runbooks, or log updates.

To solve this, Cymbal wants to integrate their entire Microsoft Graph ecosystem directly into Gemini Enterprise. As a Cloud Architect at Cymbal Group, your task is to deploy an enterprise-grade Model Context Protocol (MCP) connector. This should allow Cymbal’s Gemini Enterprise AI agents to autonomously navigate, read, and safely modify documents, while enforcing strict corporate governance through native Action Approval workflows.

Your challenge
As an AI Infrastructure Engineer, you need to configure, deploy, and securely link a custom Microsoft Graph MCP connector to Gemini Enterprise. To succeed, you must meet the following objectives:

Configure identity and security delegation within Microsoft Entra ID.
Deploy the MCP Server container to Google Cloud Run to expose the required API endpoints.
Register and authenticate the custom MCP server as an enterprise data store within the Google Cloud Console.
Link the data store to Gemini Enterprise and activate the correct read/write action permissions.
Topics tested:
Build and deploy a custom MCP server as a Google Cloud Run service.
Configure and register a custom MCP data source in Gemini Enterprise.
Secure the connection using OAuth 2.0 client credentials.
Enable 12 read-and-write actions for SharePoint and OneDrive.
Register and test the data store with Gemini Enterprise prompts.
Setup and requirements
Prerequisites and account hygiene
Because all participants share a single Microsoft 365 tenant with elevated privileges (Cloud Application Administrator), strict account hygiene and tenant isolation rules apply:

Browser Isolation: You must sign in to both Google Cloud and Microsoft Entra ID using a clean Incognito / InPrivate browser window to prevent credential caching and session collisions with your corporate or personal accounts.
Rotating Weekly Credentials: Your assigned Microsoft 365 / Entra ID credentials are temporary and strictly bound to the current week's cohort. Access is valid for one week only, after which credentials are revoked, active sessions are terminated, and the tenant environment is recycled.
First-Login Setup: On your first sign-in to the Microsoft Entra Admin Center, you will be prompted to complete a mandatory password reset and may be required to configure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). Keep your updated password accessible for the remainder of the lab.
⚠️ Account Usage & Compliance Policy:

Do not perform any extra administrative tasks, modify tenant-wide security policies, or run unauthorized Microsoft Graph API calls outside the instructions in this lab manual.

Unapproved administrative actions or high-frequency API polling can trigger automated Microsoft platform fraud detection and Smart Lockouts, which will lock out your account and disrupt the shared tenant for the entire cohort.
Pre-provisioned SharePoint environment
All SharePoint team sites (configured as public within the organization) and sample test documents (Cymbal_Helix_Upgrade.docx, Cymbal_Orion_Enablement.pptx, etc.) are already pre-created and populated for you.

Do NOT create new SharePoint sites or upload test files from scratch.
Locate your assigned Microsoft Entra credentials (shared via classroom chat) and verify that you can access the pre-provisioned SharePoint sites below before starting:
Cymbal Group Marketing
Cymbal Group Finance
Cymbal Group Operations
Note: If you encounter any issues logging into the Microsoft Entra Admin Center or accessing the pre-provisioned SharePoint sites above, please notify in the cohort chat immediately before the lab begins.

