Task 1. Register the application in Microsoft Entra ID
To allow the MCP connector to securely access Cymbal's corporate documents, you must register a Microsoft Entra ID OAuth application. Because all participants share a single directory with Cloud Application Administrator privileges, you must strictly isolate your application registration.

Strict Non-Interference Warning:

You have visibility over other participants' app registrations in this tenant. Do NOT modify, regenerate secrets, change redirect URIs, or delete any application that does not belong to you. Doing so will immediately break that participant's lab.
Mandatory Naming Convention:

You must prefix your app registration name with your assigned LDAP / username prefix (for example, <your-ldap>-cymbal-ge-mcp-app) so that your application is uniquely identifiable in the shared directory.
In the Microsoft Entra Admin Center, register a new application with the following settings:

Name: <your-ldap>-cymbal-ge-mcp-app (Replace <your-ldap> with your assigned username/LDAP prefix, e.g., jsmith-cymbal-ge-mcp-app)

Redirect URI:

https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/oauth-redirect
Copied!
Add the following Microsoft Graph Delegated API permissions and click Grant admin consent for [Tenant]:

Files.ReadWrite.All
Sites.ReadWrite.All
User.Read
Navigate to Certificates & secrets and create a new Client secret.

Copy and save the following credentials immediately for your environment configuration:

Application (client) ID (Verify this matches your <your-ldap>- prefixed app)
Directory (tenant) ID
Client Secret Value
Task 2. Configure the Gemini Enterprise app
Enable the necessary APIs
In the Google Cloud console, select your project.
In the search bar at the top, type Agent Platform, and select it from the results.
On the Overview page, click Enable APIs.
Click Enable.
Create a Gemini Enterprise app
In this challenge, you must configure a Gemini Enterprise app and enable authentication.

Create a Gemini Enterprise app using the required configuration values.
Configure the authentication settings for the global location.
Enable Google Identity as the identity provider.
Use the following configuration values during setup:

Parameter	Value
App name	gemini-enterprise-app
App ID	gemini-enterprise-app
Location	global
Identity provider	Google Identity
After completing the configuration, verify the following:
The Gemini Enterprise app has been created successfully.
Authentication is enabled for the global location using Google Identity.
Click Check my progress to verify the objective.
AT ID: 1 - Configure the Gemini Enterprise app

Task 3. Build and deploy the MCP server to Cloud Run
Next, you set up the environment variables and deploy the pre-configured Node.js MCP server code to Google Cloud Run.

Open the Cloud Shell and run the following commands to download and unzip the pre-configured Node.js MCP server code.
gcloud storage cp gs://"bucket-name"-bucket/sharepoint-mcp-server.zip .
Copied!
  unzip sharepoint-mcp-server.zip
  cd sharepoint-mcp-server
Copied!
Update the .env file in the root directory of your project using the credentials from your <your-ldap>-cymbal-ge-mcp-app Entra app registration and the pre-provisioned SharePoint root instance URL:
  MS_GRAPH_TENANT_ID="your-entra-tenant-id"
  MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_ID="your-entra-client-id"
  MS_GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET="your-entra-client-secret"
  SHAREPOINT_INSTANCE_URL="https://googlecorp.sharepoint.com"
Copied!
💡 SharePoint Instance & Site Lookup:

Because the SharePoint team sites (Cymbal Group Marketing, Cymbal Group Finance, and Cymbal Group Operations) and their document libraries are pre-provisioned in the shared tenant, look up and use your assigned SharePoint root instance URL (e.g., https://googlecorp.sharepoint.com) or assigned site URL rather than creating a new SharePoint site.
Note: Please make sure you are using the client secret value from your own prefixed app registration, not the Secret ID.
Make the deployment script executable and run it to deploy the server container to Cloud Run:
  chmod +x deploy.sh
  ./deploy.sh
Copied!
Once the deployment finishes, copy the live Cloud Run Service URL from the terminal output (e.g., https://sharepoint-mcp-server-850431687571.us-central1.run.app).
Click Check my progress to verify the objective.
AT ID: 2 - Build and deploy the MCP server to Cloud Run

Task 4. Configure the data store and enable MCP actions
Now, register the deployed Cloud Run instance as a custom Model Context Protocol data source in Gemini Enterprise.

In the Google Cloud Console, navigate to Gemini Enterprise -> Data stores -> Create data store.

Type MCP in the search bar and select Custom MCP Server.

Fill out the Connection Profile exactly as outlined below (replace {YOUR_TENANT_ID} with your Entra Tenant ID):

Parameter	Configuration
MCP Server URL	https://sharepoint-mcp-server-xxxxxxxxxxxx.us-central1.run.app/mcp
Authorization URL	https://login.microsoftonline.com/{YOUR_TENANT_ID}/oauth2/v2.0/authorize
Auth URL Parameters	&access_type=offline&prompt=consent
Token URL	https://login.microsoftonline.com/{YOUR_TENANT_ID}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Client ID	Enter Application (client) ID from your <your-ldap>- Entra app
Client Secret Value	Enter Client Secret Value from your <your-ldap>- Entra app
Scopes	https://graph.microsoft.com/.default
Note: If you receive the error AADSTS900144: The request body must contain the following parameter: 'scope'., update Auth URL Parameters to &access_type=offline&prompt=consent&scope=https://graph.microsoft.com/.default.
Note: Please make sure you are using the client secret value, not the ID.

Also, you can copy the MCP server URL from the deployment script's terminal output in the previous step. Make sure to append /mcp to the end of the URL.
Click Login to authenticate using your assigned weekly Microsoft 365 cohort account (ensure this popup opens within your clean Incognito/InPrivate session), grant permissions, and click Continue.

Name the Data Connector Cymbal Universal Data Connector, and click Create.

Wait a few minutes for initialization. Once ready, click on your new MCP data store and navigate to the Actions tab.

By default, all actions are disabled. Select all read and write actions and click Enable actions.

Click Check my progress to verify the objective.
AT ID: 3 - Configure the data store and enable MCP actions

Task 5. Link the connector to a Gemini Enterprise app
Now, bind your newly authorized data store to your active Gemini Enterprise application environment.

Click Check my progress to verify the objective.
AT ID: 4 - Link the Connector to a Gemini Enterprise app

Verification
Open your application URL (https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/home/cid/...).

Click the Connector icon inside the chat bar, authorize the server, and test the capabilities using the natural language prompts in the section that follows.

Read actions (Instant, interruption-free streaming)
1. Search SharePoint sites

Allows the AI agent to discover relevant corporate SharePoint sites across your organization based on keywords or department names.

Search for SharePoint sites related to Cymbal Group Operations.
Copied!
2. List document libraries

Retrieves all available document repositories and drives within a specific SharePoint team site.

List all document libraries in my Cymbal Group Finance site.
Copied!
3. List library items (files & folders)

Explores the directory structure, listing all files, subfolders, and metadata within a specific drive or folder location.

List all files and folders inside my Documents library in the Cymbal Group Finance site.
Copied!
4. Get file metadata

Retrieves detailed properties for any specific file, including creation date, last modified time, file size, and web URLs.

Get the metadata and last modified time for Cymbal_Helix_Upgrade.docx
Copied!
5. Read document content

Streams clean, extracted text directly to the AI agent from Word documents (.docx), PowerPoint presentations (.pptx), Excel spreadsheets (.xlsx), and text files for instant summarization or analysis.

Read the text content of Cymbal_Helix_Upgrade.docx and give me a 3-bullet summary.
Copied!
6. Get secure download URL

Generates temporary, secure, authenticated direct download URLs for any document in your repository.

Generate a direct download URL for my SharePoint presentation titled: Cymbal_Orion_Enablement.docx
Copied!
